<title>SINGAPORE: IPC offers Intel MMX-based products.</title>
<headline>IPC offers Intel MMX-based products.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-01-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Singapore's personal computer company IPC said on Thursday it was offering Intel's latest MMX technology Pentium processor on its range of computers for the home and corporate markets.</p>
<p>The MMX chip, launched on Wednesday, is a new chip that supports multimedia functions, including voice and audio data processing.</p>
<p>The MMX technology is available on IPC's 166 MHz and 200 MHz Pentium processor PCs.</p>
<p>--Singapore newsroom (65-8703080)</p>
</text>
